                <pb facs="0592" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1733: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-29T15:00:00-05:00">February 29, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Your 74, February 28, 9 p.m. Francis White states that the Council has
                    refrained from all comment of any type whatsoever, formal or informal, as
                    regards the possibility of a debt settlement with Brazil.</p>
                <p>Please correct Bouças’ impression and, if necessary, any impression that Aranha
                    may have to the contrary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
